{
  "comment": "The self-hosted embedding models the Kudos pilot compares (genki issue 92). Each gets an embedding server (embed_server.py) on `server`, its own platform and knowledge databases, its own API on `api`, a dataset digdir/kudos-next-<key> and a service kudos-pilot-<key>-retrieve-only. `prompts` are the model's own query/document prompts from its config_sentence_transformers.json; genki puts them before each text. `dtype` and `batch` are the server's; `maxBatch` keeps one embedding call under ~25 s on an M3 Pro. `mlx`: the pages are embedded on MLX first (pre_embed.py, Qwen3 architecture only). `trustRemoteCode`: the model loads Python code from its repository, read and pinned at `revision` (and `codeRevision` for code in another repository). `venv`: the Python environment in .data that serves the model, when not embed-venv (gte's 2024 code needs transformers 4.x; see the README). `round`: 2 for the models added in the second round; their bootstrap draws come from their own random sequence, so the first round's published intervals stay as they were. Round 3 adds `name` (the label in reports, when it differs from `hf`), `shortenedFrom` (a model whose stored page vectors are cut to `dimensions` by shorten.py, while the server cuts the questions the same way) and `catalogModel` (an embedding model already in genki's catalog, such as foundry/text-embedding-3-small: no local server).",
